a german car manufacturer's vision of  the future  cars are quiet environmentally sound and  electric  traffic flows unimpeded because  everything is networked with everything  else  but the reality on the road today is  still traffic jams noise and exhaust  researchers engineers and designers have  been tinkering with new ideas in  mobility for a long time and german  companies want to be global players in  the field the german government has set  an ambitious goal  by the year 2020 it wants to see a  million electric cars on german roads  the plan foresaw 100 000 electric cars  in the country already this year but  when 2014 began there were just 12 000  electric vehicles registered in germany  green mobility is still a distant ideal  on german roads in fact some of  germany's european neighbors are way  ahead  for example 6.1 percent of the vehicles  newly licensed in norway in 2013 were  electric or hybrid cars  5.6 percent of the new cars sold in the  netherlands were with france far behind  at 0.8  but in germany only 0.2 percent of newly  licensed cars were electric  and that even though german car  manufacturers are investing huge sums on  research and development  bmw has spent billions developing and  producing elegant electric cars  but german drivers aren't living the  dream of electromobility
 

